From e36c0c7a3ce907cdd7be99c777bd51416f20c11b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:16:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 81/85] hw/misc: MCP4921 12-bit SPI DAC and the DAC Click

The MCP4921 (DS21897B section 5): sixteen-bit writes (A/B, BUF, GA#,
SHDN#, twelve data bits) load the input register on CS# rising, fewer
clocks abort, LDAC# low (or falling) copies it to the DAC register;
VOUT = VREF * D / 4096, twice that with GA# low, limited to VDD, 0 V
while shut down. QOM: "vref", "vdd", read-only "code", "vout" (mV) and
"readout" for front ends.

DAC Click v100: CS# with R4 100 kOhm pull-up, LDAC# tied low, VREF on
VCC (3.3 V).

qtests: gain 1 and 2, the VDD limit, an aborted write and shutdown on
the MC00's EXT1; a write through SPI0 on the AVR64EA48 Nano Base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
